  Also removed [38;5;153mnotes[39m from [38;5;153mschema.sql[39m, since the README says that file is kept in sync with the migrations by hand.

  Two things worth knowing before the deploy job runs this against the 48,000-row production table:

  - The drop is irreversible — the [38;5;153mnotes[39m data is gone with no down migration. Worth a backup or a one-off export first
    if anyone might want it back.
  - [38;5;153mALTER TABLE ... DROP COLUMN[39m needs SQLite 3.35+ (2021). On anything older it fails outright and the table rebuild
    dance is required instead.

  I didn't run anything; there's no test or migration runner in the repo.

